From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:25:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: order rx descriptor reads after the DMA done
 check

mt76_dma_dequeue() checks MT_DMA_CTL_DMA_DONE and mt76_dma_get_buf()
then reads the length, info and buf1 words of the same descriptor, with
nothing ordering the loads. Descriptor rings are coherent DMA memory,
which on non-coherent SoCs such as MT7986 is mapped as normal
non-cacheable memory, where loads may be reordered: the other fields
could be read before the device's final write to them.

Add the dma_rmb() Documentation/memory-barriers.txt prescribes after
seeing the ownership bit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dma.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dma.c b/dma.c
index a67880a9..3aef3583 100644
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -622,6 +622,8 @@ mt76_dma_dequeue(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_queue *q, bool flush,
 			 !(q->desc[idx].ctrl & cpu_to_le32(MT_DMA_CTL_M_DONE)))
 			return NULL;
 #endif
+		/* read the rest of the descriptor only after DMA_DONE */
+		dma_rmb();
 	}
 done:
 	q->tail = (q->tail + 1) % q->ndesc;
